<title>UK: BAA SAYS AIR CARGO UNAFFECTED BY BA STRIKE.</title>
<headline>BAA SAYS AIR CARGO UNAFFECTED BY BA STRIKE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's airport operator BAA Plc said on Wednesday the volume of air cargo tonnage was unaffected by the British Airways cabin crew strike in July.</p>
<p>BAA said its seven airports handled a total 130,430 metric tonnes of cargo in July, up 7.1 percent.</p>
<p>Figures released by the authority showed Heathrow airport increased by 11.8 percent metric tonnes of cargo handled to 98,319 in July.</p>
<p>Stansted airport handled 10,223 metric tonnes in July, up 16.2 percent, but Gatwick airport showed a 14.5 percent decline to 19,551 metric tonnes.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
